remain outstanding.\\\",\\ndocs/keepalive/Observability_Contract.md:1:# Keepalive Observability Contract (Goals & Plumbing Update)\\ndocs/keepalive/Observability_Contract.md:3:**Status:** Canonical reference for keepalive behavior and on‑run observability  \\ndocs/keepalive/Observability_Contract.md:11:Keepalive must iteratively nudge a PR toward acceptance by:\\ndocs/keepalive/Observability_Contract.md:37:- `agents:keepalive` — enable keepalive on this PR  \\ndocs/keepalive/Observability_Contract.md:45:Every **keepalive instruction** comment MUST include (top of body):\\ndocs/keepalive/Observability_Contract.md:46:<!-- codex-keepalive-marker --> <!-- codex-keepalive-round: <N> --> <!-- codex-keepalive-trace: <opaque-trace-id> -->\\ndocs/keepalive/Observability_Contract.md:99:**Preconditions:** `agents:keepalive` present; human @agent activation; Gate may be pending.\\ndocs/keepalive/Observability_Contract.md:151:- `missing-label` — `agents:keepalive` absent  \\ndocs/WORKFLOW_AUDIT_2025-12-25.md:25:| Agents Keepalive Loop | 49 | 43 | 0 | 87.8% | ✅ Working |\\ndocs/keepalive/Keepalive_Reliability_Plan.md:1:# Keepalive Reliability Plan\\ndocs/keepalive/Keepalive_Reliability_Plan.md:4:**Related:** `docs/keepalive/Observability_Contract.md` (required one‑line summaries)\\ndocs/keepalive/Keepalive_Reliability_Plan.md:6:This plan closes the remaining reliability gaps in the keepalive pipeline by removing unsafe assumptions, adding a token‑free fall‑back path, and making every decision point machine‑auditable from the Checks UI.\\ndocs/keepalive/Keepalive_Reliability_Plan.md:26:- **Activation fallback (Gate):** if the Gate script didn’t supply `activation_comment`, fetch most‑recent *human* `@agent` comment (excluding keepalive‑authored comments with hidden markers).\\ntests/workflows/fixtures/keepalive/paged_comments.json:15:        \\\"agents:keepalive\\\"\\ndocs/llm-task-analysis.md:9:The keepalive automation now uses LLM-powered task completion detection to determine if a Codex session has completed its assigned task. This replaces simple regex-based heuristics with intelligent analysis of session transcripts.\\ndocs/llm-task-analysis.md:75:The keepalive loop script (`keepalive_loop.js`) displays analysis results in PR comments:\\ndocs/llm-task-analysis.md:169:1. Updated `keepalive_loop.js` with Task Analysis section\\ndocs/llm-task-analysis.md:209:Test PR in Manager-Database: #136 (`test/langchain-keepalive` branch)\\ndocs/keepalive/GoalsAndPlumbing.md:1:# Keepalive — Goals & Plumbing (Canonical Reference)\\ndocs/keepalive/GoalsAndPlumbing.md:3:> **Audience:** Human maintainers and automation agents responsible for the keepalive workflow. Review this document **before** touching any keepalive logic or dispatch plumbing.\\ndocs/keepalive/GoalsAndPlumbing.md:26:- **Purpose:** Maintain a safe, iterative loop where keepalive nudges an agent through small, verifiable increments on a PR until every acceptance criterion is complete—while guaranteeing predictable behaviour and safety rails.\\ndocs/keepalive/GoalsAndPlumbing.md:27:- **Scope:** Activation requirements, dispatch plumbing, throttling, branch-sync guarantees, and shutdown rules for the GitHub PR keepalive workflow.\\ndocs/keepalive/GoalsAndPlumbing.md:28:- **Non-goals:** Guidance for automation unrelated to keepalive.\\ndocs/keepalive/GoalsAndPlumbing.md:38:5. **Definition of done:** As soon as the acceptance criteria are all checked complete, keepalive posts no further rounds.\\ndocs/keepalive/GoalsAndPlumbing.md:45:Keepalive **must not** dispatch an agent unless *all* conditions hold:\\ndocs/keepalive/GoalsAndPlumbing.md:63:If any requirement fails, keepalive stays silent—no PR comments. Operators may record the skip reason in run summaries only.\\ndocs/keepalive/GoalsAndPlumbing.md:78:- Respect the stronger `agents:pause` label, which blocks *all* keepalive activity.\\ndocs/keepalive/GoalsAndPlumbing.md:82:1. Investigate the failure reason in the keepalive summary comment\\ndocs/keepalive/GoalsAndPlumbing.md:87:Or manually edit the keepalive summary comment to reset `failure: {}` in the state marker.\\ndocs/keepalive/GoalsAndPlumbing.md:93:When preconditions are missing (labels absent, Gate not green, run cap reached), keepalive must not add new PR comments. At most, log a concise operator summary explaining the skipped action.\\ndocs/keepalive/GoalsAndPlumbing.md:102:2. **Agent-agnostic prompt:** The base prompt (`.github/codex/prompts/keepalive_next_task.md`) is agent-agnostic—no `@codex` or agent mentions.\\ndocs/keepalive/GoalsAndPlumbing.md:135:The keepalive loop routes to different agent workflows based on the `agent:*` label:\\ndocs/keepalive/GoalsAndPlumbing.md:159:- **No self-cancellation:** Configure concurrency as `keepalive-{pr}` with `cancel-in-progress: false`.\\ndocs/keepalive/GoalsAndPlumbing.md:161:- **Summary comment:** Update the keepalive summary comment with iteration status, agent output preview, and failure tracking.\\ndocs/keepalive/GoalsAndPlumbing.md:168:- To reset failure count: edit the keepalive summary comment and set `failure: {}` in the state marker, or remove `needs-human` label.\\ndocs/keepalive/GoalsAndPlumbing.md:169:- Keepalive stands down when **all acceptance criteria are checked complete**. At that point the orchestrator stops issuing further rounds.\\ndocs/keepalive/GoalsAndPlumbing.md:175:The Keepalive workflow depends on the **Automated Status Summary** block in the PR body to extract Scope, Tasks, and Acceptance Criteria.\\ndocs/keepalive/GoalsAndPlumbing.md:180:3. **Keepalive Execution:** The keepalive loop extracts tasks from the Automated Status Summary and injects them into the agent prompt via the task appendix.\\ndocs/keepalive/GoalsAndPlumbing.md:185:- **No Tasks:** If no checkboxes are found, keepalive will stop with reason `no-checklists`.\\ndocs/keepalive/GoalsAndPlumbing.md:191:Keepalive now has two ways to detect task completion and keep PR checkboxes in sync:\\ndocs/keepalive/